{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For the sons of Simeon, by their count</b> — the lamed is bent downward, because [the prince] of his tribe, Zimri son of Salu, sinned, and they fell from his tribe. And the lamed is taller than all the letters — therefore his tribe diminished, for it produced neither king nor judge. The second lamed, of גלגלותם of Simeon, is shaped like a drawer and upright, and has no cap on its head, because the prince of the house of the father instructed Simeonite licentiousness in Israel with uncovered head and upright posture."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:01.334450450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}